    "description": "This circular walk explores Corrvaddy Woods near Letterkenny in County Donegal. The woodland lies a short distance south west of the town and is managed as a community forest with a network of waymarked trails. The paths pass through mixed planting, including native broadleaf trees and areas of conifer, with sections of open ground that give views towards the surrounding hills of east Donegal. The terrain is gently undulating, with forest tracks and narrower earth paths weaving between mature trees and younger regeneration. The woods provide habitat for common woodland birds and small mammals, while the quieter setting offers a contrast to the nearby urban area. The looped layout allows for a straightforward walk entirely within the forest boundary.You can continue your walking around Letterkenny atLough Fern,Lough MourneorGartan Lough.",
